      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "(c) 2005 Wiley-Liss, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "This is a case report on the ability of 16-slice computed tomography in assessing the patency of coronary stent and diagnosing an asymptomatic stenotic lesion with soft plaque morphology. These findings were confirmed with a selective coronary angiography. Identification of lesion morphology facilitated our decision on prophylactic and direct stenting to the lesion."
      },
